cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite them."
title: "Exact fiber elimination for the Levi--Civita convexity gates of the planar restricted three-body problem"
authors:
  - family-names: Grisa
    given-names: César Augusto
    affiliation: "Universidade Federal Fluminense"
    email: cagrisa@id.uff.br
version: "1.3.2"
date-released: "2026-07-08"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - restricted three-body problem
  - Levi-Civita regularization
  - strict convexity
  - global surface of section
  - Birkhoff conjecture
  - computer-assisted proof
abstract: >-
  Computer-assisted strict-convexity certification of the regularized energy
  surfaces of the planar circular restricted three-body problem reduces to the
  positivity of two scalar gates over a four-dimensional domain (a two-dimensional
  Levi-Civita base times a fiber angle). This package proves four exact algebraic
  identities that eliminate the fiber angle in closed form, reducing both gates to
  the two-dimensional base, together with a global floating-point reconnaissance of
  Levi-Civita convexity across the mass-energy plane and a fine-structure analysis
  showing the non-convexity is confined to a single simple fold on a radially
  star-shaped base.
